{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320870-can-x-awaken","id":1320870,"title":"Can X awaken?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-25T18:30:40-07:00","id":1320870,"title":"Can X awaken?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I dont know if this counts as errata or as a question, but Signs of Sorcery p.129 states that:<br /> <br /> <i>...some games model characters that might Awaken with<br /> templates and unique mechanics, while other games<br /> use Merits to represent near-human beings that certainly<br /> won\u2019t. Hunters with Endowments representing<br /> equipment, for example, could Awaken, while ghouls<br /> could not. Wolf-blooded can (though they lose their<br /> Wolf-Blooded Merits and tells when Awakening),<br /> while Stigmatics cannot.</i><br /> <br /> I would like help interpreting this text, <b>when it says games, does it mean gamelines, or particular games of a group?</b> I am curious since Wolf Blooded are able to keep their tell after transforming into another creature (WtF p.300), and some Demon fluff describes a mage that was an Stigmatic (Splintered City p.66):<br /> <br /> <i>Moore doesn\u2019t know it, but he was<br /> stigmatic before Awakening.</i><br /> <br /> Thanks for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-26-2019, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T21:02:01-07:00","id":1320885,"title":"","content":"It would appear that Wolf-Blooded loosing their Tells is a change in tack, or may have been put in for WtF without consulting Dave.<br /> <br /> Games does appear to imply gamelines though, WtF, VtR, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T23:37:09-07:00","id":1320904,"title":"","content":"This will not be changing. <br /> <br /> edit: to clarify, it's on the level of... Hypothetical example. If a book from a different line had casually mentioned &quot;Traditions&quot; or &quot;coincidental magic&quot; in the background of a character, it wouldn't be an erratum for a mage book. It'd just be a mistake.<br /> <br /> The character's background in Splintered City is a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 06-26-2019, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T00:50:20-07:00","id":1320909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320870-can-x-awaken?p=1320904#post1320904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will not be changing.<br /> <br /> edit: to clarify, it's on the level of... Hypothetical example. If a book from a different line had casually mentioned &quot;Traditions&quot; or &quot;coincidental magic&quot; in the background of a character, it wouldn't be an erratum for a mage book. It'd just be a mistake.<br /> <br /> The character's background in Splintered City is a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div><s>Thanks Dave, quick question, is it possible for a Mage to become a Stigmatic AFTER awakening?</s><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> important questions: can Wolf-blooded be Proximi? If so, do they retain their tells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Original question waa idiotic 06-26-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T09:32:44-07:00","id":1320977,"title":"","content":"What kind of messed up bloodline would a proximus wolfblooded have. Also afaik you get the Proximus template at birth, doesn't the wolfblooded merit require you to have no other supernatural templates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T09:53:51-07:00","id":1320978,"title":"","content":"Acrozatarim made one on his Patreon, the Carvers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T11:19:24-07:00","id":1320996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320870-can-x-awaken?p=1320978#post1320978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acrozatarim made one on his Patreon, the Carvers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, also a wolf-blooded mage, Agnes. This small inconsistencies are like an itch in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T11:27:43-07:00","id":1320998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320870-can-x-awaken?p=1320996#post1320996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, also a wolf-blooded mage, Agnes. This small inconsistencies are like an itch in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's effectively homebrew, Acrozatarim's been pretty clear that none of his stuff posted here is canon (outside of the open dev peeks). And the books are pretty clear that the only canon is what you want, your own game can only have Changelings as a supernatural without any of the other gamelines existing.<br /> <br /> I'll personally just be having Tells stay. Problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2019, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}